<title>DENMARK: Danish Wise Men see fewer jobless in 1996.</title>
<headline>Danish Wise Men see fewer jobless in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The independent Danish Economic Council said in its biannual report on Wednesday that it expected a 1996 jobless total of 245,000 and 236,000 in 1997, down from its last forecast and lower than the actual 1995 total of 288,400.</p>
<p>In its previous report last May, the council, known as the Wise Men, predicted 264,000 unemployed in 1996 and 265,000 in 1997.</p>
<p>Unemployment in September this year was 234,700 or 8.4 percent of the workforce.</p>
<p>--Steve Weizman, Copenhagen newsroom +45 33 969650</p>
</text>
